%[text] %[text:anchor:H_51183E7B] **Before you get started:**
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_51CEAF47] #### **Code hidden statements:**
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_BF646A47] This live script is intended to be used with the code hidden. On the **View** tab of the MATLAB toolstrip, in the **View** section, select **Hide Code**.  Alternately, select **Hide Code** using the icon ![live script code hidden icon](text:image:694e) at the top right of the Live Editor pane.
%[text] ![Lightbulb mark](text:image:6c01) Although the code is hidden, some interactivity requires familiarity with MATLAB. If you need more instruction, consider taking [MATLAB Onramp](https://matlabacademy.mathworks.com/details/matlab-onramp/gettingstarted), a free 2 hour online tutorial that teaches the essentials of MATLAB.
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_8F8A032D] ![Warning symbol](text:image:3535)   For an optimal experience, follow the instructions and steps in the given sequence. Proceed to a new section only after completing the preceding one. Some sections depend on variables created in prior sections and will generate errors if run out of order.
%[text] The ![Try this icon](text:image:97ae)  and  ![Exercise icon](text:image:20f6) icons refer to two different types of interactive activities that you will find in this script. The ![Try this icon](text:image:20a3)  usually indicates an interaction where you will explore the visualization of some concept introduced in this script. The ![Exercise icon](text:image:55f1) interactions are designed to challenge your understanding of those concepts and may be used for grading and completion checks by your professor.
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_7CAB0192] #### Code visible statements:
%[text] This live script is intended to be used with the code visible and output inline. On the **View** tab of the MATLAB Toolstrip, in the **View** section, select **Output Inline**. Alternately, select **Output Inline** using the icon ![live script output inline icon](text:image:1081) at the top right of the Live Editor pane.
%[text] ![Lightbulb mark](text:image:0c59) Interacting with this live script will build some familiarity with MATLAB as concepts and commands are introduced together. If you need more instruction, consider taking [MATLAB Onramp](https://matlabacademy.mathworks.com/details/matlab-onramp/gettingstarted), a free 2-hour online tutorial that teaches the essentials of MATLAB.
%[text] ![Warning symbol](text:image:81cc)   For an optimal experience, follow the instructions and steps in the given sequence. Proceed to a new section only after completing the preceding one. Some sections depend on variables created in prior sections and they will generate errors if run out of order.
%[text] The ![Try this icon](text:image:12b1)  and  ![Exercise icon](text:image:78cb) icons refer to two different types of interactive activities that you will find in this script. The ![Try this icon](text:image:04c8)  usually indicates an interaction where you will explore the visualization of some concept introduced in this script. The ![Exercise icon](text:image:6871) interactions are designed to challenge your understanding of those concepts and may be used for grading and completion checks by your professor.
